WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.769
This was locker room talk, I'm not proud of
it.

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:07.360
We've seen him rate women on their appearance.

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:11.309
Let’s pretend for a moment that the biggest
headlines out of Sunday night’s

00:00:11.309 --> 00:00:16.709
presidential debate had nothing to do with sexual assault allegations, or non-handshakes,

00:00:16.709 --> 00:00:19.040
or threats to jail political opponents—

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.280
but instead were about policy.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.840
In that bizarre alternative universe, what
would we actually learn?

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.280
Well, last night we learned the two exhausted
political parties have nothing much left

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.780
except critiques about how lousy the other one is.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.500
Some of which were, to be honest, pretty good.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:37.760
Including for Mr. Deplorable himself.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.250
She talks in favor of the rebels.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:40.550
She doesn't even know who the rebels are.

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:43.329
Look what she did in Libya with Gaddafi.

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:47.490
And sure enough, when the most hawkish Democrat
this side of Joe Lieberman talked about her

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:51.090
solutions for the war-torn Middle East, it
was a word-salad of

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.220
“safe zones” and “no-fly zones”

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.960
and wishing really hard that good things
would happen.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:01:02.360
I hope by the time I am president, that we
will have pushed ISIS out of Iraq.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:05.560
You can see the same dynamic at play with
Obamacare.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.930
Trump rightly points out the problems:

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:11.270
Their method of fixing it is to go back and
ask congress for more money.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.549
More and more money.

00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:15.079
We have right now almost $20 trillion in debt.

00:01:15.079 --> 00:01:18.639
And Clinton responds with boilerplate blather:

00:01:18.639 --> 00:01:22.639
let's fix what's broken about it, but let's
not throw it away

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.960
and give it all back to the insurance companies.

00:01:24.969 --> 00:01:28.470
So, what’s President Trump’s solution?

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:35.790
We have to repeal it and replace it with something,
absolutely much less expensive

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:37.480
and something that works.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:41.110
As for Syria, it’s hard to decipher Trump’s
exact position;

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:45.060
except for that he definitely hasn’t talked to Mike Pence any time recently.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.100
He and I haven't spoken and I disagree. I disagree.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.240
I think we have to knock out ISIS.

00:01:50.249 --> 00:01:52.249
Hillary Clinton was at her best Sunday night

00:01:52.249 --> 00:01:55.140
when explaining why Donald Trump was not fit to be president,

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.480
a judgment with which I and
about half the Republican caucus in the Senate

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.200
at this point agree.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:04.579
Donald Trump was at his best when pointing
out that the policies Clinton has supported

00:02:04.579 --> 00:02:08.649
have not been good for the country, something
I wish more Democrats would admit.

00:02:08.649 --> 00:02:11.989
But is there a positive case for Hillary being
fit for the White House?

00:02:11.989 --> 00:02:15.920
Are there Trump policies that are gonna turn
this mother around?

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:17.220
No.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.020
Of course not.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:20.920
What were you thinking?

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.580
It's just awfully good that someone with the
temperament of Donald Trump

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.680
is not in charge of the law of our country.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:29.850
Because you'd be in jail.

